[
    {
        "content": "<p>What's the current most efficient way to build up a string from parts in Lean? Apparently there used to be a <code>String.Builder</code> library function that no longer exists?</p>",
        "id": 596106852,
        "sender_full_name": "Greg Shuflin",
        "timestamp": 1779182367
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Every <code>String</code> acts like a (persistent) builder data structure by default.</p>",
        "id": 596110349,
        "sender_full_name": "Henrik Böving",
        "timestamp": 1779183202
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"395550\">Henrik Böving</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/String.20builder.20patterns/near/596110349\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Every <code>String</code> acts like a (persistent) builder data structure by default.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>so naively building up a mutable String in a do-block is efficient?</p>",
        "id": 596116998,
        "sender_full_name": "Greg Shuflin",
        "timestamp": 1779184748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">for</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"m\">1000000</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"a\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">length</span>\n\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">time</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- 235ms on live.lean-lang.org</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">eval</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">foo</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 596118042,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1779184939
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(this is using the interpreter, it will be faster when compiled)</p>",
        "id": 596118192,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1779184970
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>And for large strings, this is faster than building a list then joining?</p>",
        "id": 596308488,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1779234453
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Right now, <code>String.join</code> is just a fold over <code>(++)</code>. Of course, we might add a more optimized version in the future which preallocates the byte array, but I don't think that this will make a huge difference.</p>",
        "id": 596414276,
        "sender_full_name": "Julia Markus Himmel",
        "timestamp": 1779274194
    }
]